# What is NOT sent to the daemon for this build.
#
# BuildKit reads `<dockerfile>.dockerignore` in preference to the context root's `.dockerignore` —
# which matters here because the context is the PARENT directory of two checkouts, and no
# `.dockerignore` in either repo applies to it.
#
# Without this the daemon receives both `.git` directories and any `node_modules` a host install
# left behind: several gigabytes, uploaded before a single instruction runs, on a build that is
# already tight on disk. The Dockerfile deletes copied `node_modules` anyway; this stops them being
# transferred in the first place.

**/.git
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/build/release
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.DS_Store
**/*.vsix
**/.env
